factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 3 problems
  The headline and slides say the family is from Rasipuram ('ராசிபுரத்தின் பூர்வீகக் குடும்பம்', 'ராசிபுரத்தின் ஆர்.கே.லட்சுமண்'), but the article only says the family is Tamil-origin (தமிழகத்தை பூர்வீகமாக கொண்ட) and that he was born in Mysore; it does not say the family is from Rasipuram. Rasipuram appears only as part of his full name (ராசிபுரம் கிருஷ்ணசுவாமி லட்சுமண்).
  The reel_script says he was born in Mysore and in the same sentence says his family was from Rasipuram, which mixes place of birth and family origin; the article does not place the family's origin in Rasipuram.
  The reel_script omits that he was a cartoonist of political events and common people's problems with humour and satire, and omits the 1947 start described as a full-time cartoonist job; the reel_script also does not mention that he was the younger brother of writer R.K. Narayan, an important fact.
